.TH PREFIXPUG 1 "September 2026" "prefixpug 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prefixpug \- safe, high-performance Steam/Proton compatdata and shadercache sniffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prefixpug
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B prefixpug
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prefixpug
is a terminal utility designed to safely reclaim storage space on Linux systems by identifying and cleaning orphaned Steam/Proton compatibility data (\fBcompatdata\fR) and shader caches (\fBshadercache\fR).
.PP
Unlike generic cleanup scripts, \fBprefixpug\fR implements an uncompromising "data-loss defense" architecture:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBMulti-Library Mount Guard:\fR Verifies all mounted library folders before running. If any drive configured in Steam's \fBlibraryfolders.vdf\fR is disconnected or missing, prefixpug immediately halts to prevent misclassifying games on unmounted drives as orphans.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBNon-Steam Shortcut Parser:\fR Ingests Steam's binary \fBshortcuts.vdf\fR across all userdata accounts, protecting Non-Steam games (Battle.net, Heroic, emulation prefixes) from accidental deletion.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBInfrastructure Deny-List:\fR Permanently locks critical Proton runtime environments (Steam Linux Runtime, Proton Experimental, Proton Hotfix, Steamworks Common Redistributables) from ever being selected or purged.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBThe Pug's Nose (Save Vaulting):\fR Automatically sniffs out local save games, configurations, and user documents inside the prefix prior to any removal. Saves are archived to compressed, SHA-256-verified tarballs in \fB~/.local/share/prefixpug/backups/\fR with an uncompressed \fBmanifest.json\fR and synced to disk via \fBfsync\fR before any deletion command is issued.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBHonest Allocation Sizing:\fR Queries filesystem blocks (\fBst_blocks * 512\fR) rather than apparent file size, accurately accounting for Proton's sparse files and symlinks.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSymlink & Path Traversal Jail:\fR Never follows symlinks outside designated prefix directories. Rejects deletions if paths resolve outside \fBcompatdata/\fR or \fBshadercache/\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fB(default)\fR
Launches the interactive Synthwave Ratatui TUI dashboard. Displays disk allocation, age, detected save files, and high-value indicators (e.g., SKSE/F4SE mod loaders).
.TP
\fBscan\fR [\fI--older-than DAYS\fR] [\fI--json\fR]
Performs a read-only scan across all configured Steam libraries and prints discovered orphaned prefixes to stdout.
.TP
\fBaudit\fR
Runs a comprehensive safety diagnostic check against the local Steam environment, inspecting library mounts, Steam process lock states, active Non-Steam shortcuts, and backup directory permissions.
.TP
\fBclean\fR [\fI--dry-run\fR] [\fI--yes\fR] [\fI--purge\fR] [\fI--older-than DAYS\fR] [\fI--shaders-only\fR] [\fI--no-backup\fR]
Cleans orphaned compatdata and shader directories. By default, runs in safe \fB--dry-run\fR simulation mode unless \fB--yes\fR or \fB--purge\fR is explicitly specified.
.TP
\fBshaders\fR [\fI--yes\fR]
Zero-risk shortcut command to clean only orphaned shader caches, leaving Proton prefixes intact.
.TP
\fBvault\fR \fI<APPID>\fR
Sniffs and archives the save files for a specific AppID prefix into the backup directory without modifying or deleting the prefix.
.TP
\fBverify-backup\fR \fI<APPID>\fR
Verifies the integrity of existing backup archives for the given AppID using SHA-256 checksums and tarball structure inspection.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB-p\fR, \fB--path\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Specify an alternative Steam library path instead of auto-discovering via \fB~/.steam/root\fR.
.TP
\fB-b\fR, \fB--backup-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Specify a custom destination directory for save file backup archives (default: \fB~/.local/share/prefixpug/backups/\fR).
.TP
\fB-o\fR, \fB--older-than\fR \fI<DAYS>\fR
Filter orphans by age in days based on newest modified timestamp in the prefix.
.TP
\fB-d\fR, \fB--dry-run\fR
Simulate actions without deleting files or writing archives (default behavior for \fBclean\fR).
.TP
\fB-y\fR, \fB--yes\fR
Execute deletion without prompting for confirmation.
.TP
\fB--purge\fR
Synonym for \fB--yes\fR to execute live deletion.
.TP
\fB--shaders-only\fR
Only clean orphaned shader caches, leaving Proton prefixes intact.
.TP
\fB--no-backup\fR
Skip save file sniffing and backup archiving before deletion. \fBCAUTION: Not recommended.\fR
.TP
\fB--force\fR
Override safety guards (such as active Steam process detection). \fBUSE WITH CAUTION.\fR
.TP
\fB-j\fR, \fB--json\fR
Output scan and audit results in machine-readable JSON format.
.TP
\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
Print help information.
.TP
\fB-V\fR, \fB--version\fR
Print version information.
.SH TUI KEYBINDINGS
.TP
\fBUp / k\fR, \fBDown / j\fR
Navigate up/down in the orphan list.
.TP
\fBSpace\fR
Toggle selection of the focused item.
.TP
\fBa\fR
Select / deselect all items.
.TP
\fBs\fR
Cycle sort order (Size descending, Age oldest first, AppID ascending).
.TP
\fBm\fR
Toggle cyberpug ASCII mascot display.
.TP
\fBd\fR
Trigger cleanup of selected items (prompts with verification modal).
.TP
\fBq / Esc\fR
Exit application.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
Success / clean execution.
.TP
\fB1\fR
General execution error.
.TP
\fB2\fR
Unsafe state detected (unmounted drive, running Steam process without \fB--force\fR, escaping symlink).
.TP
\fB3\fR
User canceled or aborted prompt confirmation.
.TP
\fB4\fR
No matching orphaned prefixes found.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.steam/root/steamapps/libraryfolders.vdf\fR
Steam's library index mapping all mounted storage drives.
.TP
\fI~/.steam/root/userdata/<account_id>/config/shortcuts.vdf\fR
Steam's binary index of user-added Non-Steam shortcuts.
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/prefixpug/backups/\fR
Default directory where save file archives and manifests are stored.
.SH AUTHORS
PrefixPug Developers (GitHub: @PrefixPug).
